# PoC PARSE-012 — a char literal must be exactly one well-formed code point.
# `'\q'` is preserved by the scanner as the two bytes `\`,`q` (SCAN-011); the old
# ParseLiteral fed the buffer straight to StringUTF8ToInt and silently produced a
# wrong value. ParseLiteral now rejects anything that is not a single code point.
# EXPECT: error: single valid Unicode code point

x := '\q'
